  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is implemented. The full suite passes (1914 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**Changes**\n- **`src/click/types.py`:** new `KeyValue(ParamType[tuple[str, str]])`, placed after `UUIDParameterType`. It splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`, and an empty value is allowed (`a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`). Input with no `=` or an empty key (`abc`, `=b`) fails with `\"... is not a valid key=value pair.\"`. A value that is already a tuple passes through unchanged.\n- **`src/click/__init__.py`:** exports `KeyValue`.\n- **`docs/api.md`:** added an `autoclass` entry after `Tuple`.\n- **`CHANGES.md`:** added a \"Version 8.5.1 / Unreleased\" section at the top. There was no unreleased section before, so I created one. Adjust the version number if you use a different scheme.\n- **`tests/test_types.py`:** tests for valid parsing, failure messages, and an end-to-end `--set` option with `multiple=True` through `CliRunner`.\n\n**Not verified:** ruff and mypy aren't installed in the venv, so I didn't run the formatter, linter, or type checker. I checked line lengths by hand, and the new code is under 88 characters. The one long line (`types.py:416`) was already there.\n\nI haven't committed anything. Say if you want a commit, and I'll make it.",
